%% Reader question: Which validation data flows belong to Bazel local execution, remote cache, Build Event Service, and optional remote execution?
%% Evidence cutoff: 2026-07-11
%% Claim status: reference design; upstream BuildBuddy capability boundaries are verified, Patrick's private deployment and outcomes are not publicly reproducible
flowchart TB
    accTitle: BuildBuddy validation data flow
    accDescr: An immutable source revision enters a credential-free Bazel validation job. Bazel runs eligible actions locally, queries a trust-scoped remote cache, and emits minimized build events to a separately controlled Build Event Service. Cache hits and local action results feed tests, whose result remains bound to the source SHA. Remote execution is a separate optional path requiring explicit authorization and configuration, not an implication of cache or event ingestion.

    S["Immutable source SHA"] --> J["Credential-free CI validation job"]
    J --> B["Bazel analysis and action graph"]

    subgraph CACHE["Remote-cache path"]
      Q{"Trust-scoped cache hit?"}
      Q -->|"Yes"| C["Verified cached action result"]
      Q -->|"No"| L["Local action execution"]
      L --> W{"Trusted context may write?"}
      W -->|"Yes"| RC["Remote cache namespace"]
      W -->|"No"| N["Do not upload"]
      RC --> C
      L --> C
    end

    subgraph EVENTS["Build-event path"]
      E["Minimized and redacted build events"] --> BES["BES result and diagnostic surface"]
      BES --> O["Scoped read access, retention, deletion, and audit"]
    end

    B --> Q
    B --> E
    C --> T["Tests and validation gates"]
    T --> R["Authoritative result bound to source SHA"]

    B -. "separate explicit remote_executor path" .-> RE["Optional remote execution experiment"]
    RE -. "not implied by cache or BES" .-> C
